# SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079  -  CAT II
# All accounts installed with the web server software and tools must have
# passwords assigned and default passwords changed.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079
group:           V-206444
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    Splunk can show that no seeded installation password remains in its
                 configuration, and it can declare a password policy and force any account
                 whose password falls short of it to change that password at next login.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
governs:         user-seed.conf - The initial administrator account created on a first start.

check:           user-seed.conf [user_info] PASSWORD absent
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] forceWeakPasswordChange in true|1
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] forceWeakPasswordChange https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.2.2510/manage-credentials-and-keys/configure-a-splunk-enterprise-password-policy-using-the-authentication.conf-configuration-file
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether each existing account's password has actually been changed from
                 its installed value, which is held in the instance's user store rather
                 than in a .conf file an assessor can read.
external:        Operating system accounts created by the installation package, carried by
                 the operating system.
external:        Accounts held in the directory service where authentication is external,
                 carried by that service's own password policy.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000079 check and fix text;
                 user-seed.conf.spec:14 and 32 (PASSWORD, clear text),
                 user-seed.conf.spec:36 (HASHED_PASSWORD), authentication.conf.spec:509
                 (forceWeakPasswordChange), authentication.conf.spec:441
                 (minPasswordLength), authentication.conf.spec:514 (lockoutUsers)
finding:         A seed password remains declared in the configuration, or no password
                 policy is declared and accounts with weak passwords are not forced to
                 change them, so the application does not require installed accounts to
                 hold a changed, non-default password.
